    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Data Privacy</h1>
    <p class="law-date">Last updated: <time id="privacy-date"></time></p>
  </header>

  <article class="law-body" data-reveal>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <p>Because EasySupport is self-hosted, <strong>you</strong> are the data controller for your instance. EasySupport itself does not operate as a data controller or processor of your ticket data.</p>

    <h2>2. Data we process</h2>
    <p>EasySupport stores data you provide through your Discord guild: ticket channels, messages, user IDs, tags, roles, and module settings. All data remains in your own database.</p>

    <h2>3. Purpose of processing</h2>
    <p>Data is processed solely to operate ticketing, moderation, leveling, economy, and related guild modules for your Discord community.</p>

    <h2>4. Data retention</h2>
    <p>Data is retained until you or your staff delete tickets, guild settings, or the entire instance. Expired tickets and user data can be automatically purged (see automatic data deletion).</p>

    <h2>5. Data sharing</h2>
    <p>EasySupport does not share your data with third parties. Discord metadata (user IDs, guild IDs) is handled in accordance with Discord's Data Processing Agreement.</p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>As the instance operator, you can export, rectify, or delete any data stored in your database at any time using the built-in export and administration tools.</p>

    <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
    <p>EasySupport uses a session cookie for authentication and an optional cookie-consent cookie to remember your privacy preferences. No tracking or advertising cookies are used.</p>

    <h2>8. Contact</h2>
    <p>Data protection inquiries: <a href="mailto:privacy@example.com">privacy@example.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</section>
